<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n52767" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-Χορος,</span></b> 
		<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>with fair dancing-grounds</i>, epith. of cities, <i><span class="en">
				Od.
				11.581
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>h.Hom.</u>
				15.2
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Pi.
				<u>P.</u>
				12.26
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				E.
				<u>Heracl.</u>
				359
			</span></i> (lyr.); of Olympia, <i><span class="en">
				B.
				10.32
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀγορή</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Simon.
					164.2
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<i>of</i> or <i>for beautiful dances</i>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">στέφανοι, ἀοιδαί</span>, <i><span class="en">
				E.
				<u>Ph.</u>
				786
			</span></i> (lyr.),<i><span class="en">
				<u>Fr.</u>
				453.7
			</span></i> (lyr.); 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τρόπον τὸν καλλιχορώτατον παίζοντες</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Ar.
					<u>Ra.</u>
					452
				</span></i>
			 (lyr.); <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὁ Κ</span>., a sacred
			spring near Eleusis, <i>the fount of goodly dances,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				h.Cer.
				272
			</span></i>, cf.<i><span class="en">
				E.
				<u>Ion</u>
				1075
			</span></i> (lyr.), <i><span class="en">
				<u>Supp.</u>
				392
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				619
			</span></i> (lyr.). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>beautiful in the dance</i>, of Apollo, <i><span class="en">
				Id.
				<u>HF</u>
				690
			</span></i> (lyr.); 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κ. δελφῖνες</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					<u>Hel.</u>
					1454
				</span></i>
			 (lyr.).</div>
